.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-reset-password-request 1  "taurctl-reset-password-request " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-reset\-password\-request \- Email a reset link to the account\*(Aqs address
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl reset\-password request\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIEMAIL\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Email a reset link to the account\*(Aqs address
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIEMAIL\fR>

